    The parent listed ``name`` as a real directory, so anything but a
    real directory observed here means the path changed after the
    listing.  The name is inspected with ``fstatat`` without following
    symlinks; a symlink swapped in at this point fails the export
    identifying ``display`` as a directory that changed into a symlink,
    and any other non-directory fails saying it is no longer a
    directory.  The descriptor is then opened and proved by the shared
    :func:`_open_confirmed_directory` rule against the identity just
    observed, so a swap landing between the inspection and the open —
    link target outside the tree, inside it, or the moved original — is
    never followed.
    """
